# Annigems — Commenting Requirements

The client requires thorough commenting. Every file must be self-explanatory to a first-time reader. **Never deliver uncommented code.**

## Required minimum

- **Every class:** top docblock — what it does and its responsibility in the system.
- **Every method:** docblock — purpose, params, return, and side effects (e.g. "also writes a stock movement record").
- **Non-obvious logic blocks:** inline comment explaining **why**, not just what.
- **Every migration:** comment on table purpose and non-obvious columns.
- **Every model relationship:** short comment.
- **Form Request rules:** comment where a rule is not self-explanatory.
- **Blade files:** top comment naming the screen; inline comments around complex sections.
- **JavaScript:** comment every function and every AJAX call (endpoint + expected response).

## Example quality bar

```php
